-- Return a USER enum-with-data across the ABI. Construction lowers RIGHT n /
-- LEFT n to a BARE tag (payload discarded), so the WASM return would carry
-- only the tag while jl4-service returns {"RIGHT":{"rv":n}} — a silent wrong
-- at supported:true. FIXED (fail-closed): an @export whose GIVETH type is an
-- enum-with-data now REFUSES (supported:false → routes to the reference
-- evaluator), so this fixture is now `refused-unsupported`, NOT `differs`.
-- Kept OUT of the gated corpus (it refuses entirely, like either-shadow).
IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Rev IS ONE OF
  RIGHT HAS rv IS A NUMBER
  LEFT  HAS lv IS A NUMBER

@export return a user enum-with-data
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Rev
`mk rev` MEANS
  IF n GREATER THAN 0 THEN RIGHT n ELSE LEFT n
